WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:06.906
If March Madness teaches us one thing, there is no such thing as a sure thing.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.977
You got some picks that you think are gonna go all the way but...ehhhh?

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.245
I don’t think so.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.048
Dave, you got a lot of people that are gonna be mad

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.349
that you got their teams going out.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.052
-Yeah.
-But I’m secure in your picks 

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.253
in this hypothetical bracket.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:20.687
Mmhmm.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.721
But we have LSU—

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.456
you’ve got ‘em only going to the round of 32.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.424
What are you thinking there?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.092
Well, I mean, it starts at the top.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.362
No one knows who’s going to coach LSU.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.465
So if Will Wade is coaching, it’s one thing.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.000
And if he’s not, it’s another thing.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.103
And you saw the way that hung over their head in the SEC tournament.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.105
They went out early against Florida.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.541
And that’s gonna be something that’s gonna hold them back.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.744
The other problem with LSU, even if they didn’t have the coaching concerns,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.347
is that they’re 275th in the country in three-point shooting.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:51.251
That’s one of the things that you always look for for a high major seed.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:54.521
If they can’t shoot the threes, they get run down by a team who can.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.525
Well, it looks like Death Valley’s gonna have a whole new turn to basketball:

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.859
Tigers of LSU.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.127
But Kansas State?

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.929
We know we’re high on the mighty Anteaters

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.298
but you’ve got them going out in the first round?

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.268
Yeah, well, the Anteaters, for one thing, they’ve got Jonathan Galloway.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.502
We talked about him in the other video—

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.105
he’s a great post player, a great rim protector.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:17.243
And UC Irvine is the toughest team in the entire country to shoot twos against.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:21.548
Take that against Kansas State missing their best big man in Dean Wade

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.917
and you’ve got a recipe for an upset here

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:27.554
in what turns out to be a 13-12 matchup going into the second round.

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.823
So that looks kinda crazy for Kansas State.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.658
But Purdue, the Boilermakers

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.094
one of those blue-blood teams you always speak about—

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:34.527
Yeah.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.162
-only going to the second round.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.665
Yeah, so this is not the kind of Purdue team that you’re used to

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:43.503
 seeing with the basketball revolving around the frontcourt.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.773
Instead, they go through Carsen Edwards, who’s a great player.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.175
But they don’t have the same post presence that you’re used to seeing

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.376
and that’s gonna haunt them.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.479
They don’t get to the free-throw line a terrific amount.

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.714
And then, more than that, they’re 8-9

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.716
in road games and neutral-site games.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.918
And of course, at this point in the season

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.086
it’s all on the road.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.488
So, I like Purdue.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.223
Some people think they’re a Final Four team.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.258
I don’t think that they’re gonna make it to the second weekend.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.092
Well

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.560
you gotta be secure in your picks.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.762
And you know who not to touch in this tournament

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.332
so your bracket doesn’t go up in smoke.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.800
Choose wisely.

